<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manyema</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manyema is a region of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika">Lake Tanganyika</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba Empire</a>'s profile, Luba military expeditions extended north into Manyema during the empire's height. In the nineteenth century the region was also affected by the expansion of the East African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>.</p></div>
